{"metadata":{"name":"Sunan Ibn Majah","name_native":"Sunan Ibn Majah","section":{"24":"The Chapters on Jihad"},"section_detail":{"24":{"hadithnumber_first":2753,"hadithnumber_last":2881,"arabicnumber_first":2753,"arabicnumber_last":2881,"name_native":"The Chapters on Jihad"}}},"hadiths":[{"hadithnumber":2819,"arabicnumber":2819,"text":"It was narrated from Abu ‘Umar, the freed slave of Asma’, from Asma’ bint Abi Bakr, that she brought out a cloak edged with brocade and said:“The Prophet (ﷺ) used to wear this when he met the enemy.”","grades":[{"name":"Al-Albani","grade":"Daif"},{"name":"Muhammad Fouad Abd al-Baqi","grade":"Daif"},{"name":"Shuaib Al Arnaut","grade":"Daif"},{"name":"Zubair Ali Zai","grade":"Daif"}],"reference":{"book":24,"hadith":67}}]}